  "final_message": "Implemented all three programs. Each uses two grids for simultaneous updates and treats blocked neighbors as the cell\u2019s own value.\n\n- [Rust](/C:/Users/sandh/nb-work/39-rust-vs-python/sessions/terra/heat/rust/src/main.rs) and [plain Python](/C:/Users/sandh/nb-work/39-rust-vs-python/sessions/terra/heat/plain.py) precompute neighbor indices and stop early if the grid stabilizes.\n- [NumPy Python](/C:/Users/sandh/nb-work/39-rust-vs-python/sessions/terra/heat/fast.py) uses array operations and reusable buffers for the updates.\n\nAll three pass samples **s1, s2, and s3** byte-for-byte, plus 30 randomized cases checked against an independent reference implementation. The Rust release build completed offline.",
